WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.800
It's Tuesday, November 3, and this is the Singularity Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.300
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in superintelligence.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.320
Genius isn't cheap.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.280
Sam Altman says AI is now mostly smarter than our smartest scientists.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.530
But atoms are still atoms, he said. Power will decide what it costs.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.580
Anthropic's filing to go public shows almost $17 billion in sales,

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.140
in just three months.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.950
But it's also promised to spend nearly $900 billion, mostly on computing power.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.690
Meanwhile, Elon Musk says Grok Bot got too expensive to run.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.700
Users are hitting their limits.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.120
OpenAI says its new data centres will ease off when the grid's strained.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.500
Families shouldn't pay.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.440
Now, the big bets.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.870
Chipmaker Marvell is buying laser maker Lumentum, for $115 billion.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.530
South Korea's president says it'll double AI and chip spending next year,

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:14.050
to about $16 billion.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.840
Abu Dhabi's oil giant signed up for OpenAI's agents.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.390
Its hope? Oil field plans in hours, not months.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.480
And on Tuesday,

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:28.040
Americans in dozens of towns vote on banning or pausing data centres.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.700
Meanwhile, OpenAI built a test for everyday errands.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:39.040
Last year's model scored 49%. This year's? 80%.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.140
Like finding the right kindergarten after a move,

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.560
or a meal plan for a parent with diabetes.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.920
The catch? WIRED found over 400 apps and sites hiding abusive deepfake tools.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:56.730
And Goldman Sachs pulled AI coding tools from its bankers. Engineers only.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.500
Now, robots. About 90 teams raced them up China's sacred Mount Tai,

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.990
some carrying eggs and watermelons.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.900
A robot dog finished the climb in under 44 minutes.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.980
Most tourists take two hours.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.680
And Japan is weighing rules for self-drivin

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.480
g cars with no steering wheel and no pedals.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.110
So, genius isn't cheap. The real question is who pays,

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.050
and whether it pays us back.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.240
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.930
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.200
You've been watching the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
